    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d435">

                <pb facs="0404" n="288" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg288"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 322.112G64/1.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Minister Hartman.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 50.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-12-08">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 8, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department has received your No. 80,
                    of November 5, and your No. 82, of November 8, in regard to the desire of Mr.
                    Goo Kwai, <pb facs="0405" n="289" xml:id="pg289"/> an American citizen of
                    Chinese birth, to enter Ecuador to visit his relatives in that country.</p>
                <p>The Department has addressed to the Minister of Ecuador at Washington a note, a
                    copy of which is enclosed, in which it inquires whether he has received from his
                    Government any instructions to take up this matter with the Secretary of
                    State.</p>
                <p>Pending the receipt of a reply to that note, the Department has no instructions
                    to give the Legation in the matter, except to continue its good offices for the
                    assistance of Mr. Kwai, if occasion shall seem to permit of their exercise.</p>
                <p>As you will readily understand, the Department is compelled to take into
                    consideration in dealing with this case the legislation of the United States
                    excluding Chinese persons, in general, from this country.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
